  "assumptions": [
    "Decision dates are every calendar day of the decision month.",
    "Delivery day = the Europe/London calendar day after the decision date.",
    "The decision cutoff is configurable in the app; 10:00 Europe/London is a demo assumption, not a market rule.",
    "Forecasts are fetched by publish time from 4 days before the first decision date to the end of the last decision date, so any cutoff on any decision date can find its latest eligible publications.",
    "Forecast rows are kept if their target hour (startTime) is in a delivery day, whatever their publish time, so publications from before the decision month are not discarded.",
    "Actuals (FUELHH, fuelType WIND only) are fetched by settlement date with one day of margin each side, then filtered by startTime to the delivery days. Actuals are for evaluation only.",
    "All timestamps are parsed as timezone-aware UTC and written as ISO-8601 strings ending in 'Z'.",
    "Exact duplicate rows are removed. Conflicting actuals with different publish times keep the latest revision; any other conflict is set to missing. All conflicts are reported.",
    "Missing or invalid values are kept as missing (empty in CSV). Nothing is interpolated or filled.",
    "Rows without a usable timestamp, or off the 30-minute (actuals) / hourly (forecasts) grid, are removed and counted.",
    "Units: generation in MW (FUELHH: average MW over the half-hour; WINDFOR: hourly MW forecast).",
    "Scope: both datasets cover wind farms with operational metering on the transmission network, not total GB wind."
  ],
